---
title: Paprika
subject: dir. Satoshi Kon, 2006
genre: Anime
rating: 4.5
cover: /posters/paprika.jpg
date: 2023-01-02
excerpt: >-
  Let life take its course, it is pointless to attempt to change what cannot
  be changed.
---

Paprika is another powerful story about delusion v reality and also escapism. Similarly to Perfect Blue, our main character struggles with an internal battle of trying to figure out her true self. "Have you ever considered that you're a part of me?" Chiba deals with this self conflict and with accepting her true reality throughout the film, but ultimately, by the end of the film she comes to terms with her true self, saving the one she loves. Paprika, her alter ego, symbolizes the subconscious inside all of us. A guiding force within, that is seemingly uncontrollable. As shown by her butterfly wings, it's implied that she is the driving force inside all of us, and that it's delusional to try and control it. Let life take its course, it's pointless to attempt to change what cannot be changed.

Satoshi Kon was a master at his craft. Rest in peace.
